Yao Addington is a male gnome, bald, with a long reddish beard twisted and tied in the manner of a dwarf's. He wears heavy, oversized tactical plating that clanks with every step; unmasked, his armor is a set of interlocking hexagonal plates of a ceramic-looking kind, closer to the Scale's make than to common steel, and loud enough that he does not need stealth.

Yao is a member of [[Org/Protectorate/index|Protectorate]]. He is a friend of [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/People/Paavo Karhu|Paavo Karhu]], who shares his notion that the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] may be some living voice calling out. Yao is quiet and answers with a grunt more often than a sentence.

Yao holds the Protectorate's faith in Aurelia: the Pontifex in Calaria is a false prophet, and the true Aurelia sings out from the horizon for rescue. He hears that call in the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]], and spoke of it as a thing with intention in it. He keeps a piece of the first Aurelia's armor as a talisman, passed down from mentor to mentor back to Aurelia herself, and told [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] he might come and look at it at the fane, but that losing it would cost Anzu and his whole organization their lives. He also warned him that [[Org/Amber Call/index|Amber Call]] had come courting an alliance against the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]], and that the Protectorate had turned it down because its word was already given elsewhere.
